# Ref example

One example of the kernel reference: a name, the line that introduces it, and a
whole kernel document. No model was trained on the LOGOS kernel vernacular, so
the reference given with every prompt is held to one rule — nothing in it is
unchecked: a positive example must check, and a failure example must be refused
with the error it is shown with.

## A RefExample has:
    a name, which is Text.
    a lead, which is Text.
    a document, which is Text.
    an expectError, which is Text.

## To positiveExample (name: Text, lead: Text, document: Text) -> RefExample:
    Return a new RefExample with name name and lead lead and document document and expectError "".

## To failureExample (name: Text, lead: Text, document: Text, expectError: Text) -> RefExample:
    Return a new RefExample with name name and lead lead and document document and expectError expectError.

## Note
An example as the reference shows it: the lead, the document in a fence, and for a
failure the error the kernel gives.

## To renderExample (e: RefExample) -> Text:
    Let mutable out be e's lead + "\n\n```logos-kernel\n" + e's document + "\n```".
    If e's expectError is not equal to "":
        Set out to out + "\nThe kernel answers: … " + e's expectError + " …".
    Return out.

## Test: a positive example renders as its lead and a fenced document

Let e be positiveExample("id", "`exact` closes a goal:", "Theorem id_prop : forall (P : Prop), P -> P := by intro P h; exact h.").
Expect that renderExample(e) is equal to "`exact` closes a goal:\n\n```logos-kernel\nTheorem id_prop : forall (P : Prop), P -> P := by intro P h; exact h.\n```".

## Test: a failure example also shows what the kernel answers

Let e be failureExample("x", "A missing tactic:", "Theorem t : True := by omega.", "is not supported").
Expect that renderExample(e) contains "The kernel answers: … is not supported …".

## Test: only a failure example says what the kernel answers

For all booleans refused:
    Let mutable e be positiveExample("x", "Lead:", "Check Zero.").
    If refused:
        Set e to failureExample("x", "Lead:", "Check zero.", "Unbound variable").
    Expect that (renderExample(e) contains "The kernel answers") is equal to refused.
